meta {
  name: Refresh Connection
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{snaptradeBaseUrl}}/authorizations/{{snaptradeConnectionId}}/refresh?userId={{snaptradeUserId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Forces an intraday holdings re-pull for one connection, instead of waiting
  for the daily sync.

  Set `snaptradeConnectionId` from **List Connections** first (it is an
  authorization id, not an account id).

  Two reasons to use this sparingly:

  - **It may be billed per call** on Daily plans.
  - It does not help with transactions. Those are cached, refreshed once a day
    and delayed by a day regardless — this only freshens holdings.

  No assert on status: the endpoint is only available on some plans, so a
  non-200 here is a plan limitation rather than a failure worth flagging.
}
